{number: 81}
{title: Stand Up, Stand Up for Jesus}
{key: Bb}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Bb] Stand up, stand up for [Eb] Jesus, ye [Bb] soldiers [F7] of the [Bb] cross;
Lift high His royal [Eb] banner, it [Bb] must not [F7] suffer [Bb] loss:
From [F7] vict'ry unto [Bb] vict'ry His [Eb] army shall He [F7] lead,
Till [Bb] every foe is [Eb] vanquished, and [Bb] Christ is [F7] Lord in-[Bb] deed.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[Bb] Stand up, stand up for [Eb] Jesus, the [Bb] trumpet [F7] call o-[Bb] bey;
Forth to the mighty [Eb] conflict, in [Bb] this His [F7] glorious [Bb] day:
Ye [F7] that are men now [Bb] serve Him a-[Eb] gainst unnumbered [F7] foes;
Let [Bb] courage rise with [Eb] danger, and [Bb] strength to [F7] strength op-[Bb] pose.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[Bb] Stand up, stand up for [Eb] Jesus, stand [Bb] in His [F7] strength a-[Bb] lone;
The arm of flesh will [Eb] fail you, ye [Bb] dare not [F7] trust your [Bb] own:
Put [F7] on the Gospel [Bb] armor, each [Eb] piece put on with [F7] prayer;
Where [Bb] duty calls, or [Eb] danger, be [Bb] never [F7] wanting [Bb] there.
{end_of_verse}
